  "query_preview": "..\n\nKEY MESSAGES:\n\n- Very warm start to the week, followed by mild conditions most of\n  the week. \n\n- Break down of the ridge coming next weekend.\n\n- Snow potential coming late next weekend and early next week.\n\nWarm and dry through Friday are the expected conditions, with\ntemperatures at times running 15 to 20 degrees above normal. Today\nand Tuesday a flattening of the ridge will allow for an uptick in\nwesterly winds. \n\nThe ridge rebuilds by Wednesday with stability returning to the\nvalleys and winds becoming terrain driven. \n\nFriday a trough dropping south out of Canada will bring change to\nthe region. There are 2 features of this system that stand out,\nfirst a dramatic cool down of at least 20 degrees and potentially\nmore along with very breezy conditions. This system will come \nfrom continental Canada and be relatively dry. That said, a few \nmodel outcomes depict tropical moisture being pulled into the \ntrough, well south of our region and eventually east of the Divide.\nThen a mid-level low pressure system spins up wrapping that \nmoisture from east of the divide back into our area. More to come \nwith this system, but the potential exists that after a cooldown \nof 20 to 30 degrees a period of precipitation develops producing \nmountain snow.",
